    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Transcripts of
                    Secretary of State Kissinger’s Staff Meetings, 1973–1977, E5177, Box 8. Secret. At the
                    8 a.m. meeting on October 31, Robert H.
                        Miller, Acting Assistant Secretary of State for East Asian and
                    Pacific Affairs, said, “The Indonesian Foreign Minister is expected to open
                    talks tomorrow on Timor. The pro-Indonesian forces are gradually making progress
                    on the ground.” Kissinger
                    remarked, “It is going to wind up with Timor going to Indonesia.” Miller replied, “I think so. Maybe
                    within a couple of months.” (Ibid., Box 9)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d136-f2" n="2" xml:id="d136-f2-content">
                <p>
                    Habib and Kissinger discussed the situation
                    in Portuguese Timor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
